1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:03,962
[TIRES SCREECHING]

2
00:00:06,381 --> 00:00:07,590
[GRUNTS]

3
00:00:09,009 --> 00:00:10,260
[GRUNTS]

4
00:00:11,094 --> 00:00:12,137
Ugh!

5
00:00:13,138 --> 00:00:14,889
<i>- Boss!</i>
- [DINO GROANS]

6
00:00:14,973 --> 00:00:19,144
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

7
00:00:20,854 --> 00:00:21,813
<i>Dad?</i>

8
00:00:22,731 --> 00:00:25,066
<i>Be careful, Jordan.</i>

9
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:26,901
<i>Watch out for Caloy.</i>

10
00:00:27,485 --> 00:00:31,573
<i>Carlos-- Carlos Toledo wants to kill you.</i>

11
00:00:31,656 --> 00:00:34,451
<i>All right? Watch out for Carlos Toledo.</i>

12
00:00:34,534 --> 00:00:35,952
<i>Be careful!</i>

13
00:00:36,036 --> 00:00:38,246
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

14
00:00:38,329 --> 00:00:41,458
<i>Dad saved my life?</i>

15
00:00:41,541 --> 00:00:45,545
<i>Carlos Toledo and Dino Valentin</i>
<i>were among those who escaped.</i>

16
00:00:46,963 --> 00:00:48,673
<i>Sir, with all due respect,</i>

17
00:00:48,757 --> 00:00:50,175
<i>why didn't you tell us before?</i>

18
00:00:50,258 --> 00:00:54,429
<i>You know Jordan was one of the people</i>
<i>who got Caloy jailed.</i>

19
00:00:55,138 --> 00:00:57,557
<i>We already have leads</i>
<i>on their whereabouts.</i>

20
00:00:57,640 --> 00:00:58,725
<i>Leads?</i>

21
00:00:58,808 --> 00:01:02,812
<i>That means you're still just</i>
<i>hoping to catch them,</i>

22
00:01:02,896 --> 00:01:05,815
<i>so you're only informing us now that</i>
<i>those bastards have escaped.</i>

23
00:01:05,899 --> 00:01:08,735
<i>My boss almost got into an accident!</i>

24
00:01:09,235 --> 00:01:10,737
[WILFRED GROANING]

25
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:12,989
<i>Do you really not know where Caloy is?</i>

26
00:01:13,073 --> 00:01:14,657
<i>Believe me. Believe me.</i>

27
00:01:14,741 --> 00:01:16,785
<i>Believe me, Dino. I really don't know!</i>

28
00:01:16,868 --> 00:01:18,369
<i>If I learn that you're lying to me,</i>

29
00:01:18,453 --> 00:01:19,537
<i>you're dead.</i>

30
00:01:19,621 --> 00:01:21,414
[WILFRED CRYING]
<i>Yes! Yes!</i>

31
00:01:21,498 --> 00:01:23,917
[ROBBIE] <i>Uh, boss, have you warned Billy?</i>

32
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,668
[JORDAN]<i> Billy's already got</i>
<i>too many problems.</i>

33
00:01:25,752 --> 00:01:28,254
<i>She doesn't need</i>
<i>to know about Caloy for now.</i>

34
00:01:28,338 --> 00:01:30,298
<i>I just need to make sure she's safe.</i>

35
00:01:30,381 --> 00:01:32,383
[TIRES SCREECHING]

36
00:01:33,968 --> 00:01:35,637
- [JORDAN GRUNTS]
- [BILLY]<i> Jordan!</i>

37
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:36,763
<i>What's happening?!</i>

38
00:01:36,846 --> 00:01:38,306
<i>Relax!</i>

39
00:01:38,389 --> 00:01:40,141
<i>- Relax, okay?</i>
<i>- Oh my God.</i>

40
00:01:40,850 --> 00:01:42,685
<i>Dude, I'm sorry.</i>

41
00:01:44,938 --> 00:01:47,357
<i>Are you okay? Huh?</i>

42
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:51,027
<i>If you have a problem,</i>
<i>you can talk to me, okay?</i>

43
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:54,155
<i>You look more stressed than me.</i>

44
00:01:54,239 --> 00:01:56,699
[JORDAN] <i>Dude, I'm fine.</i>

45
00:01:58,409 --> 00:01:59,327
<i>I'm fine.</i>

46
00:01:59,410 --> 00:02:03,414
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

47
00:02:03,498 --> 00:02:05,834
POLICE

48
00:02:10,088 --> 00:02:11,381
<i>Why are you all staring at me?</i>

49
00:02:11,965 --> 00:02:14,134
<i>Hmm, I know.</i>
[SCOFFS]

50
00:02:14,634 --> 00:02:16,594
<i>You're all going to miss me!</i>

51
00:02:17,428 --> 00:02:20,849
<i>Where are you going?</i>
<i>To a mental institution as well?</i>

52
00:02:21,599 --> 00:02:24,435
<i>With your crazy mother?</i>

53
00:02:25,019 --> 00:02:26,521
<i>- What?!</i>
<i>- Who are you calling crazy?</i>

54
00:02:26,604 --> 00:02:28,940
<i>Why did they even bother</i>
<i>taking her to the hospital?</i>

55
00:02:29,023 --> 00:02:30,733
<i>- She's a lost cause!</i>
<i>- Yeah.</i>

56
00:02:30,817 --> 00:02:33,236
<i>- Just like you!</i>
<i>- A lost cause?</i>

57
00:02:33,319 --> 00:02:34,612
<i>Let's see who's really the lost cause!</i>

58
00:02:34,696 --> 00:02:36,114
[BLOW LANDS]

59
00:02:36,197 --> 00:02:42,871
- [OVERLAPPING CLAMOR]
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

60
00:02:44,956 --> 00:02:46,457
[WHISTLING]

61
00:02:46,541 --> 00:02:53,423
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

62
00:02:55,633 --> 00:02:57,760
[PRISON GUARD]
<i>Ma'am? Ma'am?</i>

63
00:02:57,844 --> 00:02:59,762
<i>Wake up, ma'am. Ma'am?</i>

64
00:02:59,846 --> 00:03:06,561
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

65
00:04:06,746 --> 00:04:07,664
[CELL PHONE CHIMES]

66
00:04:07,747 --> 00:04:09,457
BILLY: IF YOU WANT TO SLEEP
ON THE COUCH AGAIN,

67
00:04:09,540 --> 00:04:10,583
YOU'RE WELCOME TO DO SO, DUDE.

68
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:12,085
JORDAN:
BUY A SOFA BED.

69
00:04:12,168 --> 00:04:13,711
BILLY: ANY OTHER REQUESTS,
YOUR MAJESTY?

70
00:04:13,795 --> 00:04:17,882
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

71
00:04:17,966 --> 00:04:22,136
I DON'T HAVE ANY MORE
REQUESTS, YOUR M…

72
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:28,851
"So many requests. Do I need
to get a breakfast buffet too?"

73
00:04:28,935 --> 00:04:29,852
[CHIMES]

74
00:04:30,603 --> 00:04:35,441
NO NEED, MY QUEEN.

75
00:04:35,525 --> 00:04:42,198
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

76
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:46,202
JUST ALWAYS TAKE CARE OF YOURSELF.

77
00:04:48,746 --> 00:04:50,790
What's with all these requests?

78
00:04:51,624 --> 00:04:55,712
YOU'RE SO WEIRD.

79
00:04:55,795 --> 00:04:57,171
[CHIMES]

80
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:03,845
[PHONE RINGING]

81
00:05:05,888 --> 00:05:06,848
Hello?

82
00:05:06,931 --> 00:05:11,352
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

83
00:05:11,436 --> 00:05:12,353
What?

84
00:05:12,437 --> 00:05:14,939
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

85
00:05:15,023 --> 00:05:16,065
Which hospital?

86
00:05:17,317 --> 00:05:18,443
Who got hospitalized?

87
00:05:18,526 --> 00:05:21,946
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES]

88
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:23,781
HOW ARE YOU, BOSS?

89
00:05:23,865 --> 00:05:27,160
JUST MESSAGE US
IF YOU SPOT CALOY AROUND.

90
00:05:27,243 --> 00:05:29,495
WE'LL BACK YOU UP.

91
00:05:29,579 --> 00:05:32,248
I GOT THIS.

92
00:05:32,332 --> 00:05:33,666
[CHIMES]

93
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:40,423
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

94
00:05:46,763 --> 00:05:48,473
[SUSPENSEFUL STING]

95
00:05:48,556 --> 00:05:55,396
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

96
00:06:07,075 --> 00:06:08,409
[DOOR CREAKS OPEN]

97
00:06:08,993 --> 00:06:10,578
[DOOR CREAKS CLOSE]

98
00:06:10,661 --> 00:06:11,621
Jordan.

99
00:06:17,043 --> 00:06:18,461
What are you doing here?

100
00:06:19,879 --> 00:06:21,089
Um…

101
00:06:22,715 --> 00:06:24,550
I'm here to ask for your forgiveness.

102
00:06:26,344 --> 00:06:27,553
I've changed.

103
00:06:28,137 --> 00:06:29,263
I've changed, son.

104
00:06:30,348 --> 00:06:31,766
Did you break out?

105
00:06:31,849 --> 00:06:33,226
Is that what a changed person does?

106
00:06:33,309 --> 00:06:35,937
You even escaped with
Caloy Toledo.

107
00:06:36,729 --> 00:06:38,272
I'm worried about you.

108
00:06:38,356 --> 00:06:41,901
I'm sure he'll come after you.

109
00:06:41,984 --> 00:06:43,194
He'll come back for you.

110
00:06:43,945 --> 00:06:45,279
He…
[SIGHS]

111
00:06:46,030 --> 00:06:48,032
He became my friend
while we were inside.

112
00:06:48,116 --> 00:06:49,951
But I didn't know you two were enemies.

113
00:06:50,034 --> 00:06:51,994
When I found out he was planning
to do something to you,

114
00:06:52,078 --> 00:06:53,162
I followed him.

115
00:06:53,871 --> 00:06:57,250
I know I've hurt you and your mom.

116
00:06:57,333 --> 00:06:59,877
That's why I'm here now.
To make amends.

117
00:06:59,961 --> 00:07:02,713
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

118
00:07:02,797 --> 00:07:05,216
You can no longer change

119
00:07:05,883 --> 00:07:08,052
the things you did
to Mom and me back then.

120
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:11,889
<i>Dino, come on! Answer me!</i>

121
00:07:11,973 --> 00:07:14,142
<i>Are these drugs? Hey, look at me!</i>

122
00:07:14,225 --> 00:07:15,143
<i>Are these illegal drugs?!</i>

123
00:07:15,226 --> 00:07:17,770
<i>These are drugs!</i>
<i>Are you taking drugs?! Huh?!</i>

124
00:07:17,854 --> 00:07:20,148
<i>Jade, you know I have to stay up</i>
<i>all night at work, right?</i>

125
00:07:20,231 --> 00:07:22,275
- [DINO] <i>I just need it to stay--</i>
- [JADE] <i>Are you an addict?</i>

126
00:07:22,358 --> 00:07:24,318
<i>- Stay out of my business.</i>
<i>- Are you an addict?</i>

127
00:07:24,402 --> 00:07:26,946
<i>Will you please answer me?</i>
<i>Is that what you want?</i>

128
00:07:27,029 --> 00:07:28,239
<i>- To drown in them?!</i>
- [DINO] <i>Shut up!</i>

129
00:07:28,322 --> 00:07:30,575
<i>Shut up, will you?!</i>
<i>Why are you making a scene?</i>

130
00:07:30,658 --> 00:07:32,410
<i>- Why are you always meddling?!</i>
<i>- What? I'm not--</i>

131
00:07:32,493 --> 00:07:34,495
<i>- I said enough!</i>
- [GROANS]

132
00:07:34,579 --> 00:07:35,746
[THUDS]

133
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:38,374
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

134
00:07:38,458 --> 00:07:39,459
[JADE SOBS]

135
00:07:51,387 --> 00:07:52,555
[SOBS]

136
00:07:54,223 --> 00:07:55,391
[GROANS IN PAIN]

137
00:07:56,184 --> 00:07:57,226
[JADE GROANS]

138
00:08:00,021 --> 00:08:01,022
[GROANS]

139
00:08:02,315 --> 00:08:03,441
[GROANS, BREATHES SHAKILY]

140
00:08:03,524 --> 00:08:07,820
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

141
00:08:07,904 --> 00:08:10,239
I tried to go back to you in the past.

142
00:08:10,323 --> 00:08:12,408
But your grandfather
keeps on pushing me away.

143
00:08:13,284 --> 00:08:14,494
It's only right for him to do so.

144
00:08:15,828 --> 00:08:19,040
And it's only right for you
to surrender yourself to the police.

145
00:08:19,790 --> 00:08:20,791
I can't…

146
00:08:20,875 --> 00:08:23,085
Son, I can't surrender myself
to the police.

147
00:08:23,169 --> 00:08:25,546
They're targeting me.

148
00:08:25,630 --> 00:08:27,840
If I go back there, they'll kill me.

149
00:08:27,924 --> 00:08:29,592
Jordan, help me out.

150
00:08:29,675 --> 00:08:32,136
Help me make it up to you.

151
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:33,429
To turn over a new leaf.

152
00:08:33,513 --> 00:08:36,098
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

153
00:08:36,182 --> 00:08:37,558
Jordan, please.

154
00:08:38,100 --> 00:08:41,395
After everything you've done?

155
00:08:43,147 --> 00:08:44,649
What do I need to do

156
00:08:45,733 --> 00:08:48,778
to prove to you that I regret everything?

157
00:08:51,447 --> 00:08:52,406
Fine then.

158
00:08:54,158 --> 00:08:56,786
Show me where Carlos Toledo is.

159
00:08:58,371 --> 00:08:59,497
I'm sure

160
00:09:01,249 --> 00:09:02,625
you know where he is.

161
00:09:07,713 --> 00:09:08,548
Okay.

162
00:09:08,631 --> 00:09:12,635
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

163
00:09:12,718 --> 00:09:14,929
- [SOFT FOOTSTEPS]
- [TRAFFIC NOISE]

164
00:09:15,012 --> 00:09:17,348
She suffered a head trauma.

165
00:09:17,431 --> 00:09:20,268
However, we didn't find
any internal bleeding.

166
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:23,020
But she needs to be under observation

167
00:09:23,104 --> 00:09:25,815
for at least another 24 hours.

168
00:09:27,441 --> 00:09:28,484
Thank you, Doc.

169
00:09:30,278 --> 00:09:31,946
[WOMAN] Good evening, sir.

170
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:39,745
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

171
00:09:41,747 --> 00:09:43,958
[WILFRED] Here. I was able to score these.

172
00:09:44,041 --> 00:09:45,293
They're yours now.

173
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:47,587
[SIGHS] This too.

174
00:09:47,670 --> 00:09:49,130
Here's your passport and ID.

175
00:09:49,213 --> 00:09:50,339
[PAPER RUSTLING]

176
00:09:50,423 --> 00:09:51,632
These are all yours.

177
00:09:51,716 --> 00:09:53,467
[PAPER RUSTLING]

178
00:09:53,551 --> 00:09:55,845
It's dangerous for you
to stay here, Caloy.

179
00:09:55,928 --> 00:09:57,555
And for me too. So just leave.

180
00:09:58,598 --> 00:10:00,516
It'll only be dangerous
if you snitch on me.

181
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:03,394
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

182
00:10:03,477 --> 00:10:06,272
I'm sure Dino won't leave me alone.

183
00:10:06,355 --> 00:10:08,691
[SOFT RUSTLING]
[BAG ZIPS]

184
00:10:11,527 --> 00:10:13,946
He won't come after you.
Don't be a coward.

185
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:16,198
[EERIE MUSIC PLAYING]

186
00:10:16,282 --> 00:10:17,408
I can feel it.

187
00:10:19,118 --> 00:10:21,537
He doesn't believe that you're gone.

188
00:10:21,621 --> 00:10:23,789
- What if he gives the police a tip?
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

189
00:10:24,415 --> 00:10:26,417
So please, I'm begging you,
get out of here.

190
00:10:27,543 --> 00:10:33,674
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

191
00:10:33,758 --> 00:10:35,259
[CALOY EXHALES]

192
00:10:44,268 --> 00:10:45,478
[DINO] We're almost there.

193
00:10:45,561 --> 00:10:46,937
[SOFT FOOTSTEPS]

194
00:10:47,021 --> 00:10:48,314
[GUN CLINKS]

195
00:10:48,397 --> 00:10:50,900
- Hey. Put that away.
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

196
00:10:50,983 --> 00:10:53,653
What you're planning to do is dangerous.

197
00:10:55,237 --> 00:10:58,532
I don't want to call the police
if Caloy isn't even here.

198
00:10:59,283 --> 00:11:00,826
We'll find out.

199
00:11:03,287 --> 00:11:05,998
And once we're sure he's still here,

200
00:11:07,667 --> 00:11:08,709
promise me

201
00:11:10,211 --> 00:11:11,796
you'll turn yourself in to the police.

202
00:11:13,422 --> 00:11:14,632
Okay, fine.

203
00:11:16,092 --> 00:11:17,593
[TENSE STING]

204
00:11:19,595 --> 00:11:20,554
Caloy!

205
00:11:20,638 --> 00:11:26,435
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

206
00:11:37,029 --> 00:11:38,406
[METAL ROD CLINKS]

207
00:11:43,702 --> 00:11:48,040
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [ALL GRUNTING]

208
00:11:48,666 --> 00:11:50,251
- [CALOY GROANS]
- [ROD CLINKS]

209
00:11:50,334 --> 00:11:51,752
[CALOY] All right! [GRUNTS]

210
00:11:53,087 --> 00:11:54,588
[GRUNTS IN PAIN]

211
00:11:55,297 --> 00:11:56,674
[CALOY, JORDAN GRUNTING]

212
00:11:58,551 --> 00:11:59,718
[DINO GROANS]

213
00:12:04,098 --> 00:12:06,142
- [JORDAN GRUNTS]
- [CALOY GRUNTS]

214
00:12:06,225 --> 00:12:07,476
[DINO GRUNTS] Give that to me!

215
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:08,894
[DINO, CALOY GRUNTING]

216
00:12:09,562 --> 00:12:11,105
- [GUNSHOT]
- [DINO GRUNTS]

217
00:12:12,148 --> 00:12:13,649
[DINO GROANS]

218
00:12:14,942 --> 00:12:17,069
[CALOY GRUNTS IN PAIN]

219
00:12:18,988 --> 00:12:20,281
[CALOY GRUNTS]

220
00:12:20,364 --> 00:12:22,616
[GRUNTS] All right!

221
00:12:24,368 --> 00:12:26,120
- [KICK LANDS]
- [JORDAN GROANS]

222
00:12:26,203 --> 00:12:28,414
- [METAL ROD CLINKING]
- [GUNSHOTS]

223
00:12:28,497 --> 00:12:30,374
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC FADES]

224
00:12:33,961 --> 00:12:36,422
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

225
00:12:36,505 --> 00:12:38,549
[MAN] Here! I heard the gunshot here.

226
00:12:38,632 --> 00:12:40,718
- [WOMAN] Hey, hurry! Call the police.
- Stand up. Stand up!

227
00:12:40,801 --> 00:12:42,386
- Hurry!
- [DINO GRUNTING IN PAIN]

228
00:12:43,554 --> 00:12:44,597
[DINO GRUNTS]

229
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:46,307
[TENSE MUSIC FADES]

230
00:12:46,390 --> 00:12:47,641
[DINO GROANS]

231
00:12:48,350 --> 00:12:50,102
Good thing the bullet just grazed him.

232
00:12:50,186 --> 00:12:51,937
Do we need to take him to the hospital?

233
00:12:52,521 --> 00:12:54,648
No, no. I can't go to the hospital.

234
00:12:54,732 --> 00:12:56,192
Good to know,

235
00:12:56,275 --> 00:12:59,153
because I have to go somewhere.

236
00:12:59,236 --> 00:13:00,863
Take care of your father for now, okay?

237
00:13:00,946 --> 00:13:02,323
I'll go ahead.

238
00:13:02,990 --> 00:13:04,158
Thank you, son.

239
00:13:06,494 --> 00:13:07,953
I'll be back, okay? I'll be quick.

240
00:13:08,037 --> 00:13:08,871
Wait.

241
00:13:10,206 --> 00:13:12,541
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

242
00:13:12,625 --> 00:13:14,335
<i>Your grades are low again.</i>

243
00:13:14,418 --> 00:13:16,462
<i>That's from using the computer too much!</i>

244
00:13:16,545 --> 00:13:18,214
- [CRYING]
<i>- Silly thing!</i>

245
00:13:19,465 --> 00:13:20,633
[HUMS HAPPILY]

246
00:13:20,716 --> 00:13:22,718
<i>Such a smooth talker.</i>

247
00:13:24,178 --> 00:13:25,137
[CLEARS THROAT]

248
00:13:25,221 --> 00:13:30,476
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

249
00:13:30,559 --> 00:13:31,727
<i>Jade.</i>

250
00:13:32,311 --> 00:13:34,313
[DINO] <i>Jade, wait. Uhm…</i>

251
00:13:35,773 --> 00:13:37,149
<i>I'm sorry. Don't be angry.</i>

252
00:13:37,775 --> 00:13:40,319
<i>She's just my friend.</i>
<i>We were just fooling around.</i>

253
00:13:40,402 --> 00:13:43,072
<i>Don't come home to us.</i>

254
00:13:44,615 --> 00:13:46,325
<i>What are you talking about?</i>

255
00:13:46,408 --> 00:13:48,244
<i>Are you like this because</i>
<i>you're the breadwinner?</i>

256
00:13:48,327 --> 00:13:52,414
<i>Yes! You're using my money</i>
<i>to flirt with your mistress!</i>

257
00:13:52,498 --> 00:13:54,708
<i>Now you're talking to me like that?!</i>

258
00:13:54,792 --> 00:13:56,085
[JORDAN] <i>Hey! No!</i>

259
00:13:56,877 --> 00:14:03,259
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

260
00:14:18,816 --> 00:14:23,153
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

261
00:14:23,237 --> 00:14:24,822
[JADE SOBBING]

262
00:14:27,491 --> 00:14:28,617
[JADE SOBBING]

263
00:14:31,871 --> 00:14:33,289
[JADE SOBBING]

264
00:14:34,498 --> 00:14:35,708
<i>Jade, I…</i>

265
00:14:36,750 --> 00:14:40,296
<i>I got a job from Teban earlier.</i>

266
00:14:42,214 --> 00:14:43,716
<i>It was perfect timing that</i>

267
00:14:45,175 --> 00:14:47,469
<i>his wife's jeweler happened to drop by.</i>

268
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:51,181
<i>I got this for you.</i>

269
00:14:51,265 --> 00:14:54,935
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

270
00:14:56,312 --> 00:14:58,647
[JADE SNIFFLES, SOBBING]

271
00:14:58,731 --> 00:15:04,236
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

272
00:15:14,038 --> 00:15:15,289
[JADE SNIFFLES]

273
00:15:18,292 --> 00:15:19,460
[CRYING] <i>This is expensive.</i>

274
00:15:21,587 --> 00:15:23,422
<i>It's because I love you so much.</i>

275
00:15:24,298 --> 00:15:25,299
[WHISPERING] <i>I didn't…</i>

276
00:15:26,008 --> 00:15:28,886
[INHALES SHARPLY]
<i>I didn't mean to do that.</i>

277
00:15:28,969 --> 00:15:31,138
- [JADE SNIFFLES]
<i>- It won't happen again.</i>

278
00:15:32,598 --> 00:15:33,682
<i>I promise.</i>

279
00:15:34,767 --> 00:15:36,602
[JADE SOBBING]

280
00:15:36,685 --> 00:15:38,562
- [DINO WHISPERING] <i>I'm sorry.</i>
- [JADE SOBBING]

281
00:15:38,646 --> 00:15:40,272
<i>- Sorry.</i>
- [JADE SOBBING]

282
00:15:41,649 --> 00:15:43,150
[JADE SNIFFLES]

283
00:15:43,233 --> 00:15:46,820
[JADE SOBBING]

284
00:15:46,904 --> 00:15:53,327
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

285
00:16:01,418 --> 00:16:03,379
That necklace belonged to my mom.

286
00:16:05,422 --> 00:16:07,758
This is mine. Your father gave it to me.

287
00:16:07,841 --> 00:16:14,014
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

288
00:16:30,072 --> 00:16:34,785
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

289
00:16:38,956 --> 00:16:44,420
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

290
00:16:59,018 --> 00:17:00,728
[TIRES SCREECHING]

291
00:17:02,021 --> 00:17:04,648
[DINO GRUNTS]

292
00:17:05,941 --> 00:17:06,900
<i>Boss!</i>

293
00:17:09,194 --> 00:17:11,405
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

294
00:17:13,574 --> 00:17:14,533
<i>Dad?</i>

295
00:17:15,409 --> 00:17:17,786
<i>Be careful, Jordan.</i>

296
00:17:17,870 --> 00:17:19,830
<i>Watch out for Caloy.</i>

297
00:17:22,791 --> 00:17:24,752
<i>I'm here to ask for your forgiveness.</i>

298
00:17:26,879 --> 00:17:27,838
<i>I've changed.</i>

299
00:17:28,547 --> 00:17:29,965
<i>I've changed, son.</i>

300
00:17:33,302 --> 00:17:36,847
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [GRUNTING]

301
00:17:36,930 --> 00:17:39,725
[KICKS LANDING]

302
00:17:39,808 --> 00:17:42,895
[DINO GRUNTS] <i>Give that to me!</i>

303
00:17:44,354 --> 00:17:45,689
- [GUNSHOT]
- [DINO GROANS]

304
00:17:48,650 --> 00:17:54,323
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

305
00:18:06,126 --> 00:18:07,503
[WOMAN] <i>Due to</i>
<i>your withdrawal,</i>

306
00:18:07,586 --> 00:18:10,255
<i>the court dismissed Bea's cases</i>
<i>without prejudice</i>

307
00:18:10,339 --> 00:18:12,382
<i>on the grounds</i>
<i>of insufficiency of evidence</i>

308
00:18:12,466 --> 00:18:14,343
<i>and unavailability of witnesses.</i>

309
00:18:14,426 --> 00:18:16,553
<i>But we need to file for</i>
<i>medical clearance.</i>

310
00:18:16,637 --> 00:18:17,930
<i>She can come home tomorrow.</i>

311
00:18:18,013 --> 00:18:19,848
<i>Okay, Attorney. Thank you.</i>

312
00:18:26,647 --> 00:18:28,273
<i>Will you visit her, Billy?</i>

313
00:18:30,734 --> 00:18:33,445
<i>Dad's there. He can handle it.</i>

314
00:18:36,448 --> 00:18:37,449
<i>My dear.</i>

315
00:18:45,415 --> 00:18:46,416
<i>Pa.</i>

316
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:48,502
<i>Your sister called me.</i>

317
00:18:49,711 --> 00:18:51,547
<i>Atty. Granado said</i>

318
00:18:52,339 --> 00:18:54,925
you can get out
once we get your clearance.

319
00:18:58,595 --> 00:19:00,931
<i>You're not going to go</i>
<i>back to jail, dear.</i>

320
00:19:03,392 --> 00:19:05,936
<i>Like I told your sister…</i>

321
00:19:09,857 --> 00:19:13,610
<i>I don't expect you</i>
<i>to forgive me completely.</i>

322
00:19:16,947 --> 00:19:17,990
<i>But, my child,</i>

323
00:19:19,283 --> 00:19:21,660
<i>please don't waste this opportunity</i>

324
00:19:23,370 --> 00:19:25,372
<i>to start anew.</i>

325
00:19:26,915 --> 00:19:28,500
<i>I'm trying to start over too.</i>

326
00:19:31,128 --> 00:19:32,671
<i>With you.</i>

327
00:19:46,935 --> 00:19:48,729
<i>Where's my son?</i>
<i>I want to see him.</i>

328
00:19:48,812 --> 00:19:50,439
<i>See him or take him?</i>

329
00:19:50,522 --> 00:19:53,984
<i>I swore on my daughter's grave</i>
<i>that I would protect Jordan.</i>

330
00:19:54,067 --> 00:19:57,571
<i>I won't let my grandson live</i>
<i>with a father like you.</i>

331
00:20:08,081 --> 00:20:09,708
<i>Dad visited me, Gramps.</i>

332
00:20:13,712 --> 00:20:15,130
<i>He apologized.</i>

333
00:20:16,506 --> 00:20:18,008
<i>He said he'll change.</i>

334
00:20:28,227 --> 00:20:29,853
<i>Jade. Dear!</i>

335
00:20:31,897 --> 00:20:33,148
<i>Promise me…</i>

336
00:20:35,525 --> 00:20:38,487
<i>you won't let your husband</i>
<i>fool you again.</i>

337
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:41,990
<i>For your child's sake!</i>

338
00:20:45,994 --> 00:20:47,162
<i>For so long,</i>

339
00:20:48,455 --> 00:20:51,375
<i>you hid from me that</i>
<i>he was abusing you.</i>

340
00:20:53,710 --> 00:20:55,128
<i>You didn't tell me the truth!</i>

341
00:20:57,714 --> 00:20:58,882
<i>You know,</i>

342
00:20:59,675 --> 00:21:01,843
<i>I just found out recently that…</i>

343
00:21:03,887 --> 00:21:06,473
<i>we have other siblings.</i>

344
00:21:08,267 --> 00:21:09,268
<i>What?</i>

345
00:21:12,104 --> 00:21:15,857
<i>You know, I was also shocked</i>
<i>when I found out.</i>

346
00:21:18,652 --> 00:21:22,155
<i>And I know you must have</i>
<i>so many questions.</i>
